# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core 015db9951f7d42c6fc82e3baa4e5e3117268757411c27e3c3567e6a9328dec02
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile a015ac8f74c09f1939381076a27063c57235883dcd9a50b4d47635030829942a
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix e0fcfa41f9a51d2c9a3b72a829db4db18a8a7617d73aaee4cb5e6d49d3269bf2
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display 6d408d7fe1247bc18031a959ab0f99c2bc4965fd5253cd6f9f603602f253d1e9
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-curl 6d1ea4145f7a551672910e0bb49cd139f91b823ffadd48e4956a400c67034bef
